 [17592186281279 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186280230 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281279 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186280506 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281279 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186280703 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281279 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186280831 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281279 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281279 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281279 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186279770 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281279 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "faab536c-ba69-524a-89bb-9d4a9ee45c2f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281611 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186281099 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281611 #edb/ref 1069 "q-163146" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281611 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281611 #edb/ref 1071 "A rectangular plate occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3\\}$\nwith mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=(x+y)\\,\\text{kg}/{\\text{m}}^{2},$ where $x$ and $y$ area measured in meters. Find the moment of inertia of this lamina about the $y$-axis." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281611 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e73bf43d-4842-564c-b994-8b4ed88b9ee2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281611 #edb/ref 1074 "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for ${I}_{y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}(x+y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}y]}_{x=0}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}4+\\frac{8y}{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[4y+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{3}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =12+12 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia of the lamina about the $y$-axis is $24\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426079 #edb/ref 1080 "3.4\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426079 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426079 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "080d8399-ca6e-5bfc-9948-10e6f55ec587" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426082 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{22M}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426082 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426082 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1a308805-aad8-54a7-b5b1-064462e81b88" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426086 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{10M}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426086 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426086 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "21e7bd91-295b-518a-b561-81121cd85323" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426091 #edb/ref 1080 "9-4\\sqrt{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426091 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426091 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3056ba5d-f7d1-55a3-8c91-5da94f695f90" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426092 #edb/ref 1080 "5-2\\sqrt{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426092 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426092 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "32392a3b-31a7-5a44-8746-b4c85858d143" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426094 #edb/ref 1080 "13\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426094 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417